course: dictionary
lesson: 2438
title: One word, many jobs
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: Some words change their job depending on the words around them. «Patient daily care usually wins them over.» Here daily describes the care, and it means done every day, so daily is an adjective.
explain: «We feed the fish daily.» Now daily tells us how often we feed the fish, so it is an adverb meaning every day. Test it: swap in every day, and «We feed the fish every day» still makes sense, so you have the right meaning.
explain: «Multiply your daily time by 365 to see what a habit really costs.» In maths, daily means per day. Once you know the time for one day, you multiply by the number of days to find the total for a year.
fact: «Daily» means happening or done every day.
fact: «Daily» can also mean of or for one day, as in «the daily amount».
fact: As an adverb, «daily» means every day, as in «we feed the fish daily».
fact: A «daily» (noun) is a newspaper printed every day.
fact: In maths, daily means per day, so multiply by the number of days to find a total.
exercise: «Patient daily care usually wins them over.» In this sentence, what does daily mean? | Done only once, in summer | Very loud | Lost for ever | *Done every day
exercise: «We feed the fish daily.» What does daily mean here? | Once a year | *Every day | In the water | Very quickly
exercise: «Multiply your daily time by 365 to see what a habit really costs.» In maths, what is daily time? | A time that is very late | A time on a clock | *Time for one day, so you multiply to find a year's total | Time for a whole week only
test: «Dad reads the daily with his tea.» What is the daily? | A kind of bird | A bowl of soup | *A newspaper printed every day
test: «Commuting is the daily journey to and from work.» What does daily journey mean? | A journey by boat only | A journey made once in a lifetime | A journey through the night | *A journey made every day
exam: In «Plankton swim up to the surface daily», which word can replace daily without changing the meaning? | very quickly | in the summer | *every day | once a week
